{
  "note": "The contract for the design-doc parser. \"refs\" lists only the refs a fixture asserts: a missing refs key means not asserted. Refs are given after scope resolution (to is <doc id>#<item> when it resolves to another doc in the scope) and carry the 1-based line in the fixture file; they validate against $defs/ref. parent and supersedes are not refs: they are frontMatterLinks. The SND-LIB-019 entries are what validate reports; nothing from those files is stored. 010 entries name badKey, the one instance path the front matter fails at. The over-1-MiB case is not a fixture.  (PR review page spec 2026-11-04 §4, §12 Ph0). Every .md here is listed once. Item ids are in document order; parents maps an AC to its requirement; refs are {from, to, kind} with from null for the doc itself. A ref's 'to' is the item or doc#item it resolves to in its scope.",
  "roots": {
    "aw": {
      "dir": "aw",
      "scopes": "aw/<repo-slug>"
    },
    "vault": {
      "dir": "vault",
      "name": "Dock Notes"
    },
    "vault:broken": {
      "dir": "broken",
      "name": "Broken Docs",
      "note": "the broken docs; a second vault so each code's scope is its own"
    },
    "repo:harbor-web": {
      "dir": "repo",
      "docGlobs": [
        "docs/**/*.md"
      ]
    }
  },
  "vault": {
